le-playing game and the second entry in the Paper Mario series, set in a world styled to look like paper. Players guide Mario through themed locations, solving puzzles and battling enemies in a timing-based combat system where well-timed button presses strengthen attacks and defense. Battles play out on a stage before an audience whose reactions can help or hinder the player, and Mario recruits a party of companions with unique skills while equipping badges that grant new abilities. Brief segments also let the player control Princess Peach and Bowser between chapters.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 18, "name": "Science fiction"}, {"id": 27, "name": "Comedy"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/paper-mario-the-thousand-year-door", "videos": [{"id": 9911, "name": "Game intro", "video_id": "e8HxEVtxiSI", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8HxEVtxiSI", "title": "GC Paper Mario: The Thousand Year Door - Intro", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/e8HxEVtxiSI/hqdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 9912, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "aRu7uFkYdeM", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aRu7uFkYdeM", "title": "Paper Mario: The Thousand-Year Door GameCube Trailer -", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/aRu7uFkYdeM/sddefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 593, "name": "Paper Mario"}], "characters": [{"id": 1897, "name": "Voice"}]}